From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] odbccp32: SQLManageDataSources, SQLCreateDataSource, SQLGetTranslator dialogs (3672)

odbccp32: SQLManageDataSources, SQLCreateDataSource, SQLGetTranslator dialogs

The three installer dialogs are real: the ODBC Data Source Administrator (User,
System and File DSN lists with Add/Remove/Configure, Drivers, Tracing), the
Create New Data Source wizard (type, driver, Advanced keywords with Verify,
file name, review; user/system DSNs go through the driver's ConfigDSN with
ODBC_ADD_DSN, file DSNs are written as .dsn files) and the Select Translator
dialog (ConfigTranslator on the chosen translator). They read and write only
the prefix registry (Software\ODBC\...), never the host's odbc.ini files.
SQLInstallODBC stays a documented no-op: ODBC 3.x removed it.

Rebased at integration (integ-2026-10) onto earlier integration patches: clean 3-way merge.
---
diff --git a/dlls/odbccp32/Makefile.in b/dlls/odbccp32/Makefile.in
--- a/dlls/odbccp32/Makefile.in
+++ b/dlls/odbccp32/Makefile.in
@@ -1,6 +1,8 @@
 MODULE    = odbccp32.dll
 IMPORTLIB = odbccp32
-IMPORTS   = uuid advapi32
+IMPORTS   = uuid advapi32 user32 comctl32 comdlg32
 
 SOURCES = \
-	odbccp32.c
+	dialogs.c \
+	odbccp32.c \
+	odbccp32.rc
diff --git a/dlls/odbccp32/dialogs.c b/dlls/odbccp32/dialogs.c
new file mode 100644
--- /dev/null
+++ b/dlls/odbccp32/dialogs.c
@@ -0,0 +1,1241 @@
